  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$(-12)\\cdot 5=$",
  "worked_solution": "We have a product of a negative number $(-12)$ and a positive number $(5).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-12)\\cdot 5=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $12$ by $5$ without any signs: $12\\cdot 5=60.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-12)\\cdot 5=-60.\n$$",
